# Test scratch trees. These live inside the repo rather than under /tmp so
# `bunx tsc` resolves the same compiler the real check uses (#176).
#
# Each name carries an mkdtemp suffix (#323 SC-6): a fixed path is a shared
# mutable resource, and two suites or two sessions running at once write the
# same directory and delete each other's fixtures mid-assertion. That is a
# flake that looks like a logic failure, which is the hardest kind to chase —
# and the reason this project found a flake worth a PR in the first place.
.gate-vacuous-test-*/
.tree-under-test-scratch-*/
.spec-collection-scratch-*/
.state-contract-scratch-*/
.tmp-sc-drift-test-*/
.sc-arity-probe-*/
.rg713-*/

